 {
  "id": "F1",
  "title": "Landing publishes before its outer transaction commits, and never drains the feed",
  "file": "src/land/queue.ts",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "When the land queue records a merge, the 'landed' and 'merged' feed items are written but never pushed to live feed listeners such as the UI stream or an agent long-polling the feed. Those listeners stay asleep until some unrelated event happens. The run update is also sent to listeners before the landing transaction has committed, so if that transaction rolled back they would already have seen a change that never happened.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun test $TMPDIR/f1repro/f1.test.ts  (a throwaway test that runs updateLandEntry + landFeed + resolveMergedRun inside a raw store.db.transaction, exactly as LandQueue.landed() does, with a subscriber logging each message and db.inTransaction)",
    "output": "after commit: [\"run inTx=true\"]\nfeed rows: run.pr_opened,run.succeeded,land.landed,run.merged\nafter unrelated publish: [\"run inTx=true\",\"feed:land.landed inTx=false\",\"feed:run.merged inTx=false\",\"run inTx=false\"]"
   },
   "evidence": "At head, landed() does `this.store.db.transaction(() => { ... this.finish(...); for (const id of ids) this.store.resolveMergedRun(...) })()`. That raw transaction leaves pendingPublications null. updateRun/resolveRun then call chatTransaction, which publishes its buffered messages as soon as its inner savepoint returns, while the outer transaction is still open. publishFeed() starts with `if (this.db.inTransaction || this.feedPublishing) return;`, so neither chatTransaction's drain nor landFeed's drain runs, and nothing drains after the outer commit. At base, landed() called updateRun (its own top-level chatTransaction) and then finish \u2192 landFeed \u2192 publishFeed outside any transaction, so the feed was drained. The merge path drains later only if the optional metadata read returns MERGED (through fillMergedRunMetadata's chatTransaction). A PR found already merged in awaitCi, or a failed metadata read, is never drained."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "An agent watching a landing can receive a merge notification before the database commits, even if the landing subsequently rolls back. Successful landing feed items can also remain unpublished until another operation publishes something.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"${TMPDIR}/limitless-adjudication-probe.ts\" \"$PWD\"",
    "output": "F1 commit {\"delivered\":[{\"kind\":\"run\",\"inTransaction\":true}],\"persistedFeed\":[\"land.landed\",\"run.merged\"]}\nF1 after unrelated update [{\"kind\":\"run\",\"inTransaction\":true},{\"kind\":\"land.landed\",\"inTransaction\":false},{\"kind\":\"run.merged\",\"inTransaction\":false},{\"kind\":\"run\",\"inTransaction\":false}]\nF1 rollback {\"error\":\"injected second resolver failure\",\"emitted\":[{\"merged\":true,\"status\":\"resolved\",\"inTransaction\":true}],\"persistedRound\":{\"merged\":false,\"status\":\"needs_human\"},\"entry\":\"queued\"}"
   },
   "evidence": "The temporary probe invoked the actual landing method with an isolated store, subscribed to publications, and injected failure in the second merge resolver. HEAD wraps landing in `this.store.db.transaction(...)`, while store.ts:668-681 independently buffers and publishes each nested chatTransaction after its savepoint returns. Its publishFeed returns when `this.db.inTransaction` is true (line 686). Landing performs no drain after the outer commit. Base had no outer landing transaction; the equivalent successful probe delivered both feed items with inTransaction=false."
  }
