  "file": "src/land/queue.ts",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A user cancels a land entry at the moment GitHub reports the PR as merged (merged externally while the queue waited for CI, or the merge finished as the cancel arrived). The queue throws that confirmed merge away, so the runs show as unmerged until the GitHub notifier happens to reconcile them later.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun test $TMPDIR/f1repro/f23.test.ts  (F2 case: awaitCi with polling off and a client that resolves MERGED after the signal is aborted and the entry set to cancelled, then landed() is called with that observation)",
    "output": "awaitCi returned: {\"head\":\"aaaa\u2026\",\"state\":\"MERGED\",...,\"mergedBy\":{\"login\":\"owner\"},\"mergedAt\":\"2026-10-13T12:00:00Z\"}\n[land] 1: merged https://github.com/t/r/pull/1\nentry: cancelled run merged: false"
   },
   "evidence": "At head: `this.store.db.transaction(() => { if (!this.isActive(this.store.getLandEntry(entry.id) ?? entry)) return; this.finish(...); for (const id of ids) this.store.resolveMergedRun(...) })()`. The early return skips the run merge records as well as the entry transition. awaitCi returns `seen` after `await this.observe(...)` without checking the signal again, so a MERGED observation can arrive after cancel. Base's landed() called `updateRun(run.id, { merged: true })` unconditionally, so the merge was recorded (base also overwrote cancelled with landed). Cancelled entries are not resumed (start() lists only active entries). The log line still says 'merged' even though nothing was recorded."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "An operator cancels a landing while its pull-request lookup is pending, and the lookup subsequently confirms that the pull request merged. The entry remains cancelled, but the runs retain stale merge information until a separate reconciliation discovers the merge.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"${TMPDIR}/limitless-adjudication-probe.ts\" \"$PWD\"",
    "output": "F2 {\"observed\":\"MERGED\",\"aborted\":true,\"entry\":\"cancelled\",\"ownerMerged\":false,\"roundMerged\":false,\"roundStatus\":\"needs_human\"}"
   },
   "evidence": "The probe held the injected PR client's response inside the actual awaitCi method, registered its abort controller, cancelled through queue.cancel, then returned a MERGED observation and passed the result to landed. awaitCi returns that observation at line 458 despite cancellation during the await. Landing's `if (!this.isActive(this.store.getLandEntry(entry.id) ?? entry)) return;` precedes every resolveMergedRun call. Startup processes only active entries. Base recorded the merge unconditionally, although it incorrectly overwrote the cancelled entry as landed."
  }
