   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun test $TMPDIR/f1repro/f23.test.ts  (F3 case: owner run with 'Closes #42' and a review round of the same PR in needs_human; a land entry names the owner; landed() is called)",
    "output": "round prUrl: https://github.com/t/r/pull/1 status: resolved resolution: superseded merged: false\nowner merged: true"
   },
   "evidence": "At head, landed() builds `ids = [...new Set([run.id, owner.id])]` from `this.store.reviewRound(run.id)?.owner ?? run`. When the entry names the owner, ids holds only the owner, so supersedeByIssue's `!exclude.includes(r.id)` does not exclude the PR's rounds. Round prompts include the owner prompt (`reviewRoundPrompt(owner.prompt, ...)`), so they close the same issues. Base did the same through `updateRun(run.id, { merged: true })` \u2192 `supersedeByIssue(run)` with no exclusions, so this is not new. The request (merge fields, MCP approver, change-view and 401 errors) does not ask for it."
