   },
   "evidence": "For an owner-run entry, `const owner = this.store.reviewRound(run.id)?.owner ?? run; const ids = [...new Set([run.id, owner.id])];` contains only the owner. updateRun then invokes supersedeByIssue, whose exclusion check at store.ts:1892-1894 does not protect its rounds. Reconciliation calls resolveMergedRun without exclusions at github-notifier.ts:204, and already-resolved runs keep their existing resolution. Both HEAD and an isolated export of base reproduced the same owner-landing and reconciliation results. The original request specifically requires filling the parent's merge metadata; it does not explicitly require correcting this existing round-resolution behavior."
